meta {
  name: Get Sidebar Hints
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/college-admin/dashboard/sidebar-hints
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{staffAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Badge counts for the college-admin sidebar nav — how many items need
  staff attention right now, per section. All counts are college-scoped,
  computed live (no caching), each via a lightweight `count()` query
  (no row data fetched).

  Response `data`:
  {
    "newApplications": 4,           // Application.formStatus = "submitted"
    "assessmentEvaluationQueue": 2, // AssessmentAttempt.status = "under_evaluation"
    "otherRequests": 9,             // sum of everything in `breakdown`
    "breakdown": {
      "pendingEnrollment": 3,             // ApplicationCourse.status = "token_paid"
      "seatCancellations": 1,             // SeatCancellation.status = "pending"
      "courseSwitchRequests": 1,          // CourseSwitchRequest.status = "pending"
      "supportTickets": 2,                // SupportTicket.status = "awaiting_response"
      "documentSubmissionRequests": 1,    // DocumentSubmissionRequest.status = "under_review" (college -> student flow)
      "documentRequests": 1               // DocumentRequest.status = "submitted" (student -> college flow)
    }
  }

  Frontend maps each count to its own sidebar nav item's badge — see
  `getSidebarHintCount` in apps/college-admin/app/(dashboard)/layout.tsx.
  Polled every 60s client-side, not push-based.
}
